\section{Evaluation Methodology}
\label{sec:sim-and-eval}

\subsection{Sea-state ensemble and reference motion}

The evaluation uses four stationary JONSWAP seas and four Pierson--Moskowitz
seas with nonlinear Stokes harmonics (Table~\ref{tab:scenarios}).  Each
\SI{1200}{s} record is sampled at \SI{200}{Hz} and provides reference 3-D
displacement, velocity, acceleration, attitude, and corresponding body-frame
sensor measurements.  Results are scored over the final \SI{900}{s}, after
startup and one-time magnetic-reference reconfiguration.

\begin{table}[t]
  \centering
  \caption{Stationary simulation scenarios.}
  \label{tab:scenarios}
  \setlength{\tabcolsep}{5pt}
  \begin{tabular}{@{}lcc@{}}
    \toprule
    Scenario & $H_s$ [m] & $T_p$ [s] \\
    \midrule
    W1 & 0.27 & 3.0  \\
    W2 & 1.50 & 5.7  \\
    W3 & 4.00 & 8.5  \\
    W4 & 8.50 & 11.4 \\
    \bottomrule
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}

The records are directional rather than scalar heave inputs.  Figure~\ref{fig:input-spectra-3d}
shows representative frequency--direction energy densities.  JONSWAP supplies
the declared primary comparison; PM--Stokes is a separate predeclared family
testing transfer to a different spectral shape with bound harmonics.

